   "he": "זְמוֹרָה שֶׁהִיא קְשׁוּרָה כּוּ׳. קְשׁוּרָה — אִין, לֹא קְשׁוּרָה — לָא. לֵימָא מַתְנִיתִין דְּלָא כְּרַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: With regard to «a» vine «branch that is tied» to a pitcher, one may fill water with it on Shabbat. The Gemara infers: If it is «tied, yes,» it is permitted; if it is «not tied, no,» it is prohibited. «Let us say that the mishna is not in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel.»"
